\ ==== variables ====

\ globals: `variable` declares (value 0), `to` assigns and auto-creates at the
\ REPL; `variables` ( -- arr ) answers one { :name :value :type } frame per
\ global, oldest first, live values; `vars` pretty-prints them.

variables . cr                          \ [ ] (no globals at startup)

variable x
x .
42 to x
x .
99 to x
x .
variable y
"hello" to y
y .
[< 1 2 3 >] to y
y .
cr

\ === variables: one frame per global, oldest first, live values ===
variables .
variables [: :name @ :] map . cr        \ [ :x :y ]

\ constants, symbols, and colon words are not globals
symbol marker
variables size . cr                     \ 2 still (PI, E, TAU never appear)

\ composes with the dataset machinery
[ 1 2 3 ] to z
:blue to hue
variables frames>dataset 3 [ ] headn

\ === vars pretty-prints each frame ===
vars

\ === ++ / -- increment a global variable in place; ^ declares it, as `to` needs ===
variable counter
5 to counter
: bump  ^counter | ++ counter ;
: unbump  ^counter | -- counter ;
: undeclared-bump ++ counter ;          \ (error: no ^counter in the head)
bump counter . bump counter . unbump counter . cr    \ 6 7 6

clear

\ ==== to autocreate ====

\ `to` on a name that is neither a declared local nor an existing word: at the
\ REPL it auto-creates a global, inside a definition it declares a word-local.

\ auto-create on first assignment, then read
4 to x
x . cr                                  \ 4

\ reassignment of the auto-created global
9 to x
x . cr                                  \ 9

\ holds any value, not just floats
[ 1 2 3 ] to arr
arr . cr                                \ [ 1 2 3 ]

\ explicit `variable` still works alongside auto-create
variable v
5 to v
v . cr                                  \ 5

\ === inside a definition the name becomes a local ===

\ no locals list at all: the first `to` opens the frame where it stands
: implicit 1 to fresh  fresh 41 + ;
implicit . cr                           \ 42

\ captures are just `to` on the incoming values, topmost first
: hypotenuse to b to a  a a * b b * + sqrt ;
3 4 hypotenuse . cr                     \ 5

\ the slot is per call, not shared like a global would be
: counted 0 to tally  tally 1 + to tally  tally ;
counted . cr                            \ 1
counted . cr                            \ 1

\ intermediates chain, and a head list that receives grows to hold them
: chained | n | n 2 * to doubled  doubled 1 + to bumped  doubled bumped + ;
5 chained . cr                          \ 21

\ a loop body assigns the same slot each turn
: summed | n | 0 to total  0 to i
	begin i n < while  total i + to total  i 1+ to i  repeat
	total ;
5 summed . cr                           \ 10

\ a global of the same name minted later leaves the compiled local alone
7 to tally
counted . cr                            \ 1
tally . cr                              \ 7

\ code may precede the frame: the literal is emitted, then the frame, then the store
: after-code [: 3 :] execute to sprout  sprout 1 + ;
after-code . cr                         \ 4

\ a quotation declares into its own frame, not the enclosing word's
: quotation-frame [: 5 to inner  inner inner + :] execute ;
quotation-frame . cr                    \ 10

clear
\ === errors ===
\ a read of an undeclared name is still unknown — only `to` declares
: reads-unknown never-set 1 + ;

clear

\ ==== constant ====

\ constant ( value -- ): define an inline word that pushes the value as a
\ literal, so it folds into call sites instead of fetching at run time.

5 constant softening
softening .  cr
softening 3.0 f* .  cr

\ any value works, not just numbers
"abc" constant tag
tag .  cr

\ inside a compiled word the constant folds to a literal — no call, no fetch
: scale  softening 3.0 f* ;
' scale see-compiled

clear
